  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "The number of subscribers $S(t)$ to a new video streaming service after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${S}^{\u2032}(t)=0.11S(t).$ If the streaming service had $60\\,000$ subscribers after $20$ weeks, calculate the number of subscribers after $32$ weeks.",
  "worked_solution": "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nS(t)={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{0}$ is the initial number of subscribers.\n\nWe are given that after $20$ weeks, $60\\,000$ people subscribed to the service. So, substituting $t=20$ and $S(20)=60\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${S}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(20) & ={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 20} \\\\ 60\\,000 & ={S}_{0}\\,{e}^{2.2} \\\\ {S}_{0} & =\\frac{60\\,000}{{e}^{2.2}} \\\\  & \u22486\\,648.190,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nS(t)=6\\,648.190\\,{e}^{0.11t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the number of subscribers after $32$ weeks. So, substituting $t=32$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(32) & =6\\,648.190\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 32} \\\\  & =6\\,648.190\\,{e}^{3.52} \\\\  & \u2248224\\,605,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, the streaming service will have about $224\\,605$ subscribers after $32$ weeks.",
